+# Native wallet Send and atomic peer trades (v128)
+
+Use `client.value.transferCapabilities()` for truthful application readiness and `client.value.transferSource()` for an owned sender/recipient native value tuple. Preview reads require only actual read scopes. Fresh device-held proof authority grants the appropriate write scope only after an exact final review. Normal read authorization does not imply payment consent.
+
+`client.value.ownSource()` exports only the authenticated caller's actual admitted Original and current native positions, with explicit subjects.read. Peer-owned Originals are never fetched with a service-admin identity. A peer supplies their own source after choosing to participate. Account indexes and balances locate and project admitted native value; they cannot mint value or replace source admission.
+
+Direct settlement uses `client.value.planSettlement()` and `client.value.executeSettlement()`. Source/destination V123 value heads are distinct native settlement coordinates: do not compare them to generic artifact append-history heads. Reuse the exact semantic attempt and check `executionByIdempotencyKey` before retrying an unknown acknowledgement. A reported zero-write result must mean all economic writes rolled back; a lost response is unknown until recovery proves the immutable outcome.
+
+For mixed ownership/value trades, `planReceizNativeTradeV128()` freezes every native member, expected participant head, audience, commit domain and semantic attempt. `client.nativeTrade.identitySource()` creates a public-key-only identity carrier with bounded root-bound current-key lease and a real device admission signature; never send private device key/account files to a peer. `client.nativeTrade.ownershipBasis()` returns a source-admitted unsigned handoff basis with pinned KKS proof. Both device keys sign each full-plan basis. `client.nativeTrade.prepareOwnership()` seals conditional candidates only after both signatures; those candidates cannot be bearer claimed or independently moved.
+
+`client.nativeTrade.commit()` independently reopens the complete transition set and commits all ownership/value legs in one native SQL transaction. Actual current key grants are rechecked under locks. Every member moves together or all economic changes roll back. A positive result requires package-pinned root evidence over the exact complete immutable receipt and recovery, not a caller-shaped store response. `resolve()` and `recover()` preserve the same attempt and reverify complete native histories at the actually attested accepted Kai coordinate. Metadata, source self-hashes, databases, app sessions, MCP results and AI text do not create committed SDK custody.
+
+Retain `readReceizCommittedNativeTradeRecoveryProofV128(committed)` before projecting received custody. Its portable evidence includes every root acceptance and accepted predecessor. After a restart, `verifyReceizNativeTradeRecoveryProofV128(proof, {audience: "wildz"})` verifies that complete history offline and reissues SDK custody for the exact accepted candidate; it never executes a transfer, creates a device grant or requests a host. Serialized committed status, an isolated candidate or an incomplete ancestor chain must fail. Current global heads still govern new transfers and consumption.
+
+Native food/material/Honey packages originate in an accepted `client.nativeWorld.append()` event, then `packageSource()` binds their exact world package and source head into a root-accepted Original. Pending seals are unusable. `createReceizNativeWorldResourceAdoptionStepV128()` derives the recipient command only from the genuine accepted trade proof; `createReceizNativeWorldResourceUnpackStepV128()` binds the actual current package Original and its accepted history into the world command. Unpacking consumes its global custody head in the same locked world compare-and-swap transaction; rollback consumes nothing and a consumed package cannot be transferred again. Local saved portions remain display history, without silently gaining native ownership authority.
+
+MCP exposes five explicit adapters: value transfer source/capabilities, owned-source preparation, native trade commit and native trade resolve. Owned-source and commit previews perform zero effects and return an exact confirmation digest. Confirmed calls reuse only proof authority already held by the existing process-local identity exchange. Credentials, private keys, Originals and recovery bytes are removed from model output. These new financial adapters remain outside the marketplace nonfinancial execution allowlist; do not change execution profiles to evade that gate.
+
+Prerequisites: deploy the native API routes and additive native custody/world SQL migrations before testing real accounts. Never simulate deployment readiness with a fabricated accepted receipt, source position, key lease, local unsigned checkpoint or fallback in-memory recovery journal. Visual animation and input remain in the existing render loop; network/seal/SDK work runs only on explicit actions.
